@inject ApiMetadata Api
@* Banner's Overview, written by hand after Alert's: status and color, dismissing (previewed in each
   mode) and how long it's remembered, the stays-dismissed demo, its place in an app (code) and a
   banner shown later. Accessibility and See also come from the doc comment. *@

<Heading Level="2">Usage</Heading>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Usage</Code>
<TextBlock>A banner is a message about the whole app or site. It suits planned maintenance, a trial that's ending or an expired license. Put it at the top of the page, or in an <Anchor Href="docs/components/app-shell">AppShell</Anchor>, where it has a row of its own above the header. For a message about part of a page, see <Anchor Href="docs/components/alert">Alert</Anchor>.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Status and color</Heading>
<TextBlock>The status is the kind of message, and it sets the banner's color and icon. Set <Code>Status</Code> to choose one. For an announcement in your brand's color, set <Code>Accent</Code> and <Code>Icon</Code> instead.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="banner-statuses" />
<List>
    <ListItem>With <Code>Accent</Code>, the status still sets the icon and the word screen readers hear.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>Title</Code> sets a bold lead-in on the same line as the text.</ListItem>
    <ListItem>To put a link or button after the text, add a <Code>BannerActions</Code>.</ListItem>
    <ListItem><Code>Variant</Code> is <Code>Soft</Code> (the default), <Code>Outline</Code> or <Code>Solid</Code>, as on Alert.</ListItem>
</List>

<Heading Level="2">Dismissing</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dismissible banner has a close button, and once closed it stays closed on later pages. Set <Code>Dismissible</Code> to add it. The dismissal is remembered in a cookie named by <Code>RememberKey</Code>.</TextBlock>
<ExampleViewer Example="banner-dismiss" />
<TextBlock><Anchor Href="docs/common/render-modes">IzzyBlazor's script</Anchor> writes the cookie as the banner closes. The server reads it and leaves the banner out of every later page, static or interactive. Where the server can't read cookies (WebAssembly), IzzyBlazor's script hides a remembered banner as the page loads.</TextBlock>
<TextBlock>To show a new message to everyone again, give it a new key. Without a <Code>RememberKey</Code>, the key comes from the title, text and links, so changing the message does the same.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">How long it stays closed</Heading>
<TextBlock>A dismissal can last until the browser closes, for a year, or for this page only. Set <Code>Remember</Code> to choose:</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th><Code>Remember</Code></th><th>The banner stays closed</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Session</Code> (default)</td><td>Until the browser closes</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>Persistent</Code></td><td>For a year</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>None</Code></td><td>On this page only</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>
<ExampleViewer Example="banner-remembered" WidthSwitch />
<TextBlock>The server reads the cookie through <Code>AddIzzyBlazor()</Code>, from the IzzyBlazor package. On interactive pages, <Code>@@bind-Dismissed</Code> also reports a dismissal found in the cookie.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">In an app</Heading>
<TextBlock>In an AppShell, a banner has its own row above the header. To keep it in view as the page scrolls, set <Code>Sticky</Code>.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor" Title="MainLayout.razor">@InShell</Code>
<TextBlock>A sticky banner pushes the sticky header and sidebar down by its height. When the message wraps to a second line, IzzyBlazor's script measures the new height. With JavaScript off, the banner keeps room for one line.</TextBlock>

<Heading Level="2">Shown after the page loads</Heading>
<TextBlock>A banner can appear in response to something, such as a lost connection on interactive pages. Set <Code>Announce</Code> so screen readers read it out when it appears. Screen readers find a banner that's there when the page loads as a labeled region instead.</TextBlock>
<Code Block Language="razor">@Later</Code>

<Heading Level="2">Labels and localization</Heading>
<TextBlock>The banner has a region name, a word for the status, and a close button name for screen readers. To set them for the whole app, see <Anchor Href="docs/common/text">Text and other languages</Anchor>.</TextBlock>
<Prose Class="site-table ib-scroll">
    <table>
        <thead><tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Sets</th><th>Default</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
            <tr><td><Code>Label</Code></td><td>The region's name</td><td>"Announcement"</td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>StatusLabel</Code></td><td>The word read before the message</td><td>"Info", "Success", "Warning" or "Error"; none for <Code>Neutral</Code></td></tr>
            <tr><td><Code>DismissLabel</Code></td><td>The close button's name</td><td>"Dismiss"</td></tr>
        </tbody>
    </table>
</Prose>

@if (OverviewParts.Of(Component, Api).Count > 0)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Parts</Heading>
}
<OverviewParts Component="Component" />

<Heading Level="2">Mode support</Heading>
<ModeSupportTable Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@if (ApiComponent.Accessibility is not null)
{
    <Heading Level="2">Accessibility</Heading>
    <DocHtml Html="@ApiComponent.Accessibility" Context="@(Context with { Overview = true })" Size="ProseSize.Md" />
}

<Heading Level="2">Parameters</Heading>
<ParameterTable ApiComponent="ApiComponent" ApiHref="@Registry.ApiPageHref(Component)" Context="Context" Compact />

<OverviewSeeAlso Component="Component" ApiComponent="ApiComponent" />

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public RegistryComponent Component { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiComponent ApiComponent { get; set; } = null!;

    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public ApiPageContext Context { get; set; } = null!;

    private const string Usage = """
        <Banner Status="Status.Warning" Dismissible RememberKey="maintenance-2026-11">
            Scheduled maintenance on Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC.
            <BannerActions><Anchor Href="/status">Details</Anchor></BannerActions>
        </Banner>
        """;

    private const string InShell = """
        <AppShell>
            <Banner Status="Status.Warning" Sticky Dismissible
                    RememberKey="maintenance-2026-11">
                Scheduled maintenance on Sunday from 02:00 to 04:00 UTC.
            </Banner>
            <AppHeader>…</AppHeader>
            <AppSidebar>…</AppSidebar>
            <AppMain>@Body</AppMain>
        </AppShell>
        """;

    private const string Later = """
        @if (_offline)
        {
            <Banner Status="Status.Danger" Announce>
                You're offline. Changes are saved when the connection comes back.
            </Banner>
        }
        """;
}
